From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:19:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Vulkan: Minecraft's RenderDragon (functions looked up by
 name, SPIR-V in materials, the device functions bgfx needs)

Minecraft (Bedrock Edition, 1.21.120) renders with RenderDragon, Mojang's
bgfx fork, on Vulkan, and the NSP script took it for an NVN game whose
shader split found nothing.

- profile_guess.py: main imports no Vulkan function and no
  nvnBootstrapLoader; it gets vkGetInstanceProcAddr from NVIDIA's driver
  with nn::ro::LookupSymbol and the rest through it. vk_lookups counts the
  Vulkan names main keeps when it imports LookupSymbol and names
  vkGetInstanceProcAddr (141), which decides graphics vulkan.
- hle_ro.c: LookupSymbol gives the host's implementation of a vk* name no
  loaded module defines, as the host stands in for that driver.
- vk_shaders.py: the SPIR-V is in bgfx shader binaries (format 5) inside
  renderer/materials/*.material.bin and, for bgfx's own shaders, in main.
  material_modules takes a module whose u32 size prefix covers exactly its
  instructions; the NSP script passes ExeFS/main too. Each key is
  translated once (12,286 modules, 1,323 different). bgfx's clear shaders
  declare a uniform block without a binding: it gets binding 0. bgfx hands
  the bytes to vkCreateShaderModule unchanged: every module the game
  created was in the library.
- hle_vk.m: the shader table takes up to 64 resources a shader (Minecraft
  has up to 27; 24 dropped the last). bgfx gives up on the device when a
  core device function is null, so the game destroyed its device and
  recreated its vi layer every frame. Implemented: dynamic blend
  constants, vkCmdUpdateBuffer, vkCmdClearAttachments of whole targets,
  vkCmdBlitImage (one layer and level of single-sampled 2D colour
  images: a copy, or a quad sampling a 2D view of the source's layer and
  level; t_vk_blit checks layer 1 of an array, copied and scaled, under
  Metal's validation) and vkCmdResolveImage. Compute, indirect draws, vkCmdCopyQueryPoolResults
  and partial clears exist and log a [RED] line once (open).
  An integer vertex input read through an integer format of the other
  sign (the skinned actors' int bone indices fed R16_UINT) is read through
  the format of the shader's sign: Metal refused those pipelines and every
  animal and mob was missing.

With these the game plays on the Mac (world, mobs, a controller).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#1652
Reason: Minecraft (RenderDragon on Vulkan) is detected, its shaders translated and its renderer initialized
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#769

